{{Wireless adapter |brand=Tekram |model=U300C |revision=(Atmel) |upc= |ean= |asin= |price= |est_release_date= |fcc_date=02/19/2001 |manuf_country=Taiwan |manuf= |manuf_model= |manuf_rev= |availability= |if=USB |if_bus_version=1.1 |if_connector_type=Female B |form_factor=corded (modular) adapter |vendor_id=0b3b |device_id=1612 |subvendor_id= |subdevice_id= |id_string= |fcc_id=O6M-WUSB11 |ic_id= |chip1_brand=Atmel |chip1_model=AT76C503A |chip2_brand=Intersil |chip2_model=HFA3861 |chip3_brand= |chip3_model= |accessible_UART=No |flags= |ant_conn= |802dot11_protocols=b |txchains= |rxchains= |sstreams= |oui= |lin_driver= |win_driver= }} {{On at76c50x matrix}}
aka U-300C
Per [http://web.archive.org/web/20040603080142/http://www.tekram.de/sections.php?op=viewarticle&artid=36 Tekram's website (via archive.org)], there appear to be multiple revisions of the device. From the driver files, all revision prior to v2.5 are 0b3b:1612 ID devices. v2.5 devices have 0b3b:1601 IDs and use the Intersil PRISM 2.5/3 chipset. The Tekram link also includes drivers for the device (but specifies that it is without XP support).
